Subject: [PATCH] aacparse: wait for the rest of a split ADTS frame

In sync, an ADTS header passes the check without looking at the
available data. When a download chunk ends inside a frame and the part
already there reaches the minimum frame size, the frame is short and
the parser skips one byte into it: sync is lost and the whole frame is
dropped. The timestamps go on, so every dropped frame moves the audio
21 ms ahead of the video. Ask for the whole frame instead.

--- a/gst/audioparsers/gstaacparse.c
+++ b/gst/audioparsers/gstaacparse.c
@@ -1488,6 +1488,15 @@
 
   ret = framesize <= map.size;
 
+  if (!ret && aacparse->header_type == DSPAAC_HEADER_ADTS && !lost_sync
+      && !GST_BASE_PARSE_DRAINING (parse)) {
+    /* the frame goes on in the next buffer: wait for it, skipping into it
+     * would lose sync and the whole frame */
+    gst_base_parse_set_min_frame_size (GST_BASE_PARSE (aacparse), framesize);
+    *skipsize = 0;
+    goto exit;
+  }
+
   if (aacparse->header_type == DSPAAC_HEADER_ADTS) {
     /* see above */
     frame->overhead = 7;
